    "serial": {
        "baud_rate": 115200,
        "comments": "{{:media:buffalo:g300nh_a2.png?320x240&direct|Front PCB, ver2 A1 A0}}\n{{:media:buffalo:g300nh_a2_serial_port.png?320x240&direct|Serial port on PCB ver2 A1 A0}}\n\nThe slot surrounded by a square is  Pin 1 VCC +3.3V.\n\n| **Pin 1**   | VCC +3.3V      |\n| **Pin 2**   | GND            |\n| **Pin 3**   | TX             |\n| **Pin 4**   | RX             |\n| Settings    | 115200,8,N,1   |\n\nOn the WZR-300HP, Pin 1 does not supply +3.3V. There is a 0 K resistor right next to pin one which can be bridged to complete the +3.3V circuit. Unfortunately, it is covered in solder now, but I believe that it was labeled R347 on the silk screen. Once this is completed, the serial console will function. If you are using a USB TTL cable, this may not be necessary.\n\n**DO NOT CONNECT VCC**, since this will most likely irreversably damage your hardware.\n",
